    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk. i dont think it's anything specific. it's just... constant. like i'm watching my life happen from behind a thick pane of glass. i see people laughing or being excited and it feels like i'm looking at a movie in a language i don't speak. i try to force myself to feel something, even just a little bit of anger or sadness, but it's just that same heavy, empty gray. it's exhausting to pretend to be a person all day. i'm just so tired of the emptiness.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
